From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] PackageInstaller: a white header keeps its edge

patches/aosp-frameworks-base/0062 makes colorPrimary white, which takes the
grey 245 band (1072 x 95 px, measured on V86 on 2026-10-27) off the top of
every install screen. What it does not do is give the header an edge, and on
this device it never had one: the layouts set

    android:elevation="@dimen/headerElevation"

on the header and let Material's shadow mark where the chrome ends. This port
draws every window in software (docs/design/performance.md), and software
rendering draws no elevation shadow, so the only thing that ever separated the
header from the content was a grey one panel level from white -- which rule 1
of docs/design/eink-ui.md says is no separation at all.

So the header keeps its lower edge, drawn as rule 3 asks: a 2 px black rule
under the chrome's own white. Settings got the same treatment in
patches/aosp-settings/0008, with the same drawable and the same values.

One band per screen carries it -- the last one above the content, so that
stacked bands are not ruled off from each other:

  install_confirm.xml, install_success.xml, install_failed.xml,
  install_installing.xml, install_staging.xml   the app_snippet header
  install_confirm_perm.xml                      the question under the header
  install_confirm_perm_update.xml               the tab strip under both

The rule's white is ?android:attr/colorPrimary rather than a literal, so the
band stays whatever the chrome colour is. Names are added in this application
only, where adding one costs nothing: it is adding one to framework-res that
moves every resource ID after it, and with them framework.jar and the ART boot
image.

--- a/res/layout/install_confirm.xml
+++ b/res/layout/install_confirm.xml
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
     android:orientation="vertical">
 
     <LinearLayout android:id="@+id/app_snippet"
-        android:background="?android:attr/colorPrimary"
+        android:background="@drawable/pw3_bottom_rule"
         android:layout_width="match_parent"
         android:layout_height="?android:attr/actionBarSize"
         android:orientation="horizontal"
